# Pinned `spec` revision the conformance runner validates against.
#
# The runner refuses to run if the spec checkout it is given is not at this
# commit (override with --allow-spec-drift when deliberately testing against
# unreleased vocabulary). Without a pin the suite silently tracks whatever is
# on spec `main`, so a run that passed yesterday can pass today for a
# different reason.
#
# To re-pin: check out the new spec revision, put its full SHA and its
# VOCAB_VERSIONS line below, run `make -C . conformance` (or
# `scripts/run_conformance.py`), and record the resulting counts in the PR.

# Pinned at the MERGE commit of the-cascade-protocol/spec PR #31 on `main`
# (core v3.7 / health v2.8 / clinical v1.16 / coverage v1.5; tags
# `vocab/core-v3.7`, `vocab/health-v2.8`, `vocab/clinical-v1.16`,
# `vocab/coverage-v1.5`, all four of which point at this same commit).
#
# WHAT MOVING THE PIN DID TO THE PRE-EXISTING SUITE: nothing. The 136 fixtures
# that existed before this batch score 109 passed / 27 failed against BOTH the
# previous pin and this one, fixture for fixture and reason for reason. The
# release is additive and strictly widening, and that claim is now measured here
# rather than taken from the changelog.
#
# WHAT THE PIN IS CARRYING THAT THE PREVIOUS ONE COULD NOT: the 25 fixtures added
# in this PR exercise vocabulary that does not exist at d37901e. Measured
# RED-first against that commit, 19 of the 25 fail there -- every negative and
# every warning fixture among them reports NO_VIOLATION / NO_WARNING, because the
# constraint they are about had not been authored. See the Verification section
# of each INVENTORY.md for the per-fixture measurement.
#
# Re-measured at this commit with the batch in place:
# 133 passed / 28 known failures / 0 skipped / 161 total.
# The 28th known failure is new and is owned by `spec`; it is
# clinical/status-laboratoryreport-in-progress.WARN.ttl, and
# KNOWN_FAILURES.json states the defect.

